00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.190 align:start position:0%
a hero welcomed back home  images of happy soldiers returning from  the front are broadcast almost every day  on ukrainian television  but pictures like these are not shown  they were recorded just a few weeks ago  as ukrainian soldiers were surrounded by  rebels near ilovaisk  it was a brutal battle a bloodbath  medic michael gulac was in the thick of  it  he says of the 400 ukrainian troops  fighting in that battle only a third  survived  he himself was injured  we don't have proper weapons or vehicles  i belong to a special unit of the  interior ministry and we were taken to  the front in a large taxi a taxi without  breaks  my colleague colga was the driver and i  sat next to him providing cover with my  machine gun  the battle at iloveisk was the ukrainian  forces biggest defeat so far  mishael believes it was only god who  enabled him to survive not his gun or  his generals  there were 250 volunteers in our  battalion only 90 said they were  prepared to fight  the rest refused not because they were  afraid but because they were smart lots  more would have fought if they were  properly armed we barely had enough  weapons to defend ourselves let alone  launch an offensive  for days michael and his colleague  looked after the survivors of the route  they conducted operations in makeshift  facilities and public buildings  using supplies that were decades old  outside desperate troops waited for a  convoy to be evacuated to safety  many never made it  we only had two doctors for every 100  men in the battalion  the regulations say that there has to be  at least 10 doctors for every 100  soldiers  there was no transport to evacuate the  wounded  we couldn't carry them on stretchers for  20 kilometers  i felt so sorry for the wounded i  stroked them and told them everything  would be all right  even though i knew some of them would  die within minutes  what are you supposed to do this is war  a war that is still going on in spite of  the ceasefire  and a war in which a safe homecoming is  something many never get to experience  you
 

